        <span class="stripe-accent"></span>
        <h2>Symptom And Adjustment</h2>
        <p>A starting point, not a rulebook. Where two actions are given, take the first one first.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-body">
        <p>This assumes the spring frequencies are correct, the car has travel to work in, and — where fitted — high-speed compression has already been set by the procedure above. Where two actions are given, the first is almost always the one acting on the end of the car that is not doing its job.</p>

        <figure class="guide-figure">
          <figcaption>Balance traits — all four are rebound adjustments</figcaption>
